<title>SOUTH AFRICA: FORECAST - S.African economic indicators consensus.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - S.African economic indicators consensus.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following major South African economic indicators are scheduled for release next week:</p>
<p>DAY    GMT   INDICATOR    PERIOD  FORECAST   RANGE	PREVIOUS</p>
<p>MON    1200  TRADE	  OCT     +0.9BLN    0.8/1.2BLN +0.67BLN</p>
<p>THURS  0900  PPI Y/Y	OCT     +7.9	 7.8/8.1    +7.6</p>
<p>THURS  0900  PPI M/M	OCT     +1.0	 0.8/1.2    +0.4</p>
<p>THURS  1500  CURRENT ACCT Q3	  **			-4.6BLN</p>
<p>FRI    1500  RESERVES     NOV     10.38BLN   10.0/11.0  10.28BLN</p>
<p>**Reserve Bank Governor Chris Stals said on November 20 that preliminary estimates indicated a seasonally adjusted and annualised Q3 current account deficit of 10 billion rand against 16.4 billion in Q2.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
